1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,631
在你打字之前，我们的分诊页显示一行衬线字的问候
Before you type, our triage page shows a serif greeting asking where it hurts,

2
00:00:04,631 --> 00:00:09,195
问你哪里不舒服；屏幕中间是输入框，下面是一排建议
an input box in the middle of the screen, and a row of suggestions under it.

3
00:00:09,515 --> 00:00:11,947
如果你觉得它像 Claude 的 app，那就对了
If that reminds you of Claude's app, it should.

4
00:00:12,267 --> 00:00:15,531
是你要求一比一照抄的，agent 把它做了出来
You asked for a one-to-one copy, and the agent built it.

5
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:18,711
照抄，不正是做产品应该避免的吗？
Isn't copying exactly what a product should avoid?

6
00:00:19,031 --> 00:00:20,474
但这一次，照抄就是计划
Here it was the plan.

7
00:00:20,524 --> 00:00:23,484
抄了什么、拒绝了什么、我们加了什么
What was copied, what was refused, what we added,

8
00:00:23,484 --> 00:00:26,625
还有什么是还没人做过的：这就是这一集
and what nobody has built yet: that is this episode.

9
00:00:27,967 --> 00:00:29,410
先认识各个部分
First, the parts.

10
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:33,748
几乎每个聊天 app 都有同样这几样，设计师给它们都起了名字
Almost every chat app has the same ones, and designers have names for them.

11
00:00:34,068 --> 00:00:37,140
空状态，也就是首屏，是发第一条消息之前的页面
The empty state is the page before the first message.

12
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:41,898
建议是现成的问题；我们的建议点开是演示回放
Suggestion chips are ready-made questions; ours start demo replays.

13
00:00:42,218 --> 00:00:44,180
输入框就是你打字的地方
The composer is the input box.

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,812
它里面有模型菜单和发送键；等回答的时候，发送键会变成停止键
Inside it sit a model menu and the send key, which turns into a stop key while you wait.

15
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:53,277
发出去以后，你的话放在右边的气泡里
Once you send, your words sit in a bubble on the right,

16
00:00:53,277 --> 00:00:55,917
回答整宽显示，不加框
and the answer runs full width without a box.

17
00:00:56,237 --> 00:01:00,994
每条回答下面是一排操作按钮：复制；最新的一条还有重新回答
Under each answer is an action row: copy, and under the latest one, retry.

18
00:01:01,314 --> 00:01:04,962
往上翻，会出现一个圆形按钮，带你回到最下面
Scroll up, and a round button appears to take you back to the bottom.

19
00:01:05,282 --> 00:01:08,824
输入框下面还有一行小字：免责声明
And under the input, one line of fine print: the disclaimer.

20
00:01:11,367 --> 00:01:13,074
团队里没有设计师
The team has no designer.

21
00:01:13,394 --> 00:01:17,144
你要求这一页照着 Claude 的聊天界面一比一地做
You asked for the page to follow Claude's chat, one to one,

22
00:01:17,144 --> 00:01:21,213
当天夜里，agent 把理由写成了决策 0006
and that night the agent wrote the reasons down as decision six,

23
00:01:21,213 --> 00:01:22,866
并和另外两个方案做了比较
against two other options.

24
00:01:23,186 --> 00:01:28,412
自己设计一套风格：没有参考，大概率做得普通，还容易返工
Invent our own style: without references, probably ordinary, and likely to be redone.

25
00:01:28,732 --> 00:01:30,695
从几个 app 里各取所长
Take the best parts of several apps.

26
00:01:31,015 --> 00:01:34,044
或者照抄一个成熟的 app，一比一，不混搭
Or copy one mature app exactly, with no mixing.

27
00:01:34,284 --> 00:01:39,190
先停一下：为什么照抄一个产品，会比从几个产品里各取所长更好？
Before the answer: why would copying one product beat picking the best parts of several?

28
00:01:42,934 --> 00:01:48,225
因为不同产品的部件彼此不一致：间距、颜色、按钮的行为都不一样
Because parts from different products disagree: spacing, colours, how a button behaves.

29
00:01:48,545 --> 00:01:50,045
拼接的地方会露出来
The seams show,

30
00:01:50,045 --> 00:01:55,073
决策记录还指出了第二个代价：你再也说不清每个决定是从哪来的
and the decision record names a second cost: you can no longer say where each choice came from.

31
00:01:55,393 --> 00:01:59,313
一个成熟的参考，会用同一种方式回答每个小问题
One mature reference answers every small question the same way,

32
00:01:59,313 --> 00:02:03,670
所以用最少的设计判断，就能得到一个不难看、不出错的页面
so the fewest design calls give a page that is neither ugly nor wrong.

33
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:05,995
这对用的人也有好处
It also helps the people using it.

34
00:02:06,315 --> 00:02:11,022
设计师把它叫作雅各布定律：用户大部分时间都在别的网站上
Designers call it Jakob's law: users spend most of their time on other sites,

35
00:02:11,022 --> 00:02:13,590
所以他们希望你的网站也照同样的方式工作
so they prefer yours to work the same way.

36
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:18,603
agent 提议的规则是：每个界面只照抄一个参考
The rule the agent proposed: every screen copies exactly one reference.

37
00:02:18,923 --> 00:02:23,851
聊天页的参考，就是团队每个人每天都在用的 Claude 的 app
For the chat page, that is Claude's app, which everyone on the team uses every day.

38
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,800
来看抄了什么
Here is what was copied.

39
00:02:27,013 --> 00:02:30,384
一栏，最宽 768 像素
One column, at most 768 pixels wide.

40
00:02:30,704 --> 00:02:33,136
你的消息放在右边一个米灰色的气泡里
Your message in a beige bubble on the right.

41
00:02:33,456 --> 00:02:36,357
回答用衬线字，整宽，不加框
The answer in serif type, full width, no frame.

42
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:40,184
输入框：一个白色的圆角框，会随着你打字长高
The composer: a white rounded box that grows as you type.

43
00:02:40,504 --> 00:02:44,335
沿着它的下边，在 Claude 放附件和工具的位置
Along its bottom edge, where Claude keeps attachments and tools,

44
00:02:44,335 --> 00:02:49,123
我们放了三个自己的下拉菜单：谁在问、保险，以及你在哪里
we put three drop-downs of our own: who is asking, insurance, and where you are.

45
00:02:49,443 --> 00:02:54,860
右边是模型菜单，Terra，思考强度中，紧挨着陶土橙的发送键
On the right, the model menu, Terra at medium effort, next to the terracotta send key,

46
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:58,829
在 Claude 的帮助文档里，它的模型菜单也在这个位置
the same spot where Claude's help page puts its own model menu.

47
00:02:59,067 --> 00:03:02,978
这里有两个决定是你做的：要不要照抄 Claude 的聊天页
Two choices here were yours: copy Claude's chat page at all,

48
00:03:02,978 --> 00:03:07,280
以及要不要连它温暖的配色和衬线字一起抄，而不只是版式
and copy its warm colours and serif type too, not only the layout.

49
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:12,229
这些只用在这一页；网站的其他页面仍然用中性的过渡主题
They stay inside this one page; the rest of the site keeps its neutral theme.

50
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:15,892
没抄的部分，每一样都有理由
What was not copied, each for a reason.

51
00:03:16,212 --> 00:03:19,574
Claude 的标志、名字和私有字体：它们不属于我们
Claude's logo, name and private fonts: they aren't ours,

52
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:25,578
Claude 思考时显示它的标志，我们显示一个小圆点，字体用开源的
so where Claude shows its logo while it thinks, ours shows a small dot, and the fonts are open ones.

53
00:03:25,898 --> 00:03:28,982
侧栏、对话历史、附件和工具
The sidebar, chat history, attachments and tools:

54
00:03:28,982 --> 00:03:33,514
我们没有账号、没有存储，这个原型也不需要
we have no accounts and no storage, and the prototype doesn't need them.

55
00:03:33,834 --> 00:03:38,762
还有第二集讲过的两样：推理原文，以及一边写一边流出来的文字
And the two from episode two: the raw reasoning, and words streaming as they are written.

56
00:03:39,082 --> 00:03:41,130
我们的回答要先通过检查器
Our answers pass the checker first.

57
00:03:42,467 --> 00:03:44,067
再来一个更难的问题
Now a harder question.

58
00:03:44,216 --> 00:03:48,163
一位在中国的家长，打开这个页面，想了解在波士顿的孩子的情况
A parent in China opens this page about their child in Boston.

59
00:03:48,483 --> 00:03:50,680
他需要什么，是学生本人不需要的？
What do they need that the student doesn't?

60
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:58,167
先从 911 说起
Start with 911.

61
00:03:58,402 --> 00:04:00,386
家长在中国打不了 911
A parent can't dial it from China.

62
00:04:00,706 --> 00:04:04,739
所以页面上每一句固定的话，对家长都会改写
So every fixed line on the page changes for parents:

63
00:04:04,739 --> 00:04:10,711
不是让你打 911，而是请孩子或身边的人在当地打 911
instead of call 911, it asks the child or someone nearby to call 911 locally.

64
00:04:11,031 --> 00:04:14,530
电话号码前面加上国家码 1，并注明从中国拨打
Phone numbers get a plus one and the words dial from China.

65
00:04:14,850 --> 00:04:20,439
急救和危机热线干脆不做拨号链接，只写：请当地的人来打
Emergency and crisis numbers get no dial link at all, only: ask someone there to call.

66
00:04:20,684 --> 00:04:22,561
有些新增是给所有人的
Some additions are for everyone.

67
00:04:22,881 --> 00:04:26,433
紧急情况下，红框的「现在就做」排在最前
In an emergency, a red do-this-now block comes first,

68
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:29,985
立刻全部显示，读屏软件会马上念出来
appears at once, and is read aloud by screen readers.

69
00:04:30,305 --> 00:04:33,591
顶栏一直有一个紧急情况的入口
An emergency link sits in the top bar at all times.

70
00:04:33,911 --> 00:04:36,635
演示和估算都标着模拟
Demos and estimates are labelled simulated,

71
00:04:36,635 --> 00:04:42,337
学生把回答复制给家长时，标注也一起带走：不是诊断
and when a student copies an answer for a parent, the label goes with it: not a diagnosis.

72
00:04:42,584 --> 00:04:46,071
还有一些是给用不同方式使用页面的人
And some are for people who use the page differently:

73
00:04:46,071 --> 00:04:49,295
读屏软件可以按隐藏的标题一轮一轮地跳
hidden headings a screen reader can jump between,

74
00:04:49,295 --> 00:04:53,375
依据链接至少 24 像素高，手指点得准
source links at least 24 pixels tall so a finger can hit them,

75
00:04:53,375 --> 00:04:54,954
放大到 400% 时
and at 400 percent zoom,

76
00:04:54,954 --> 00:04:58,968
页面从顶上开始，紧急情况的入口就在眼前
a page that opens at the top with the emergency link in view.

77
00:05:00,317 --> 00:05:01,917
agent 是怎么把它做出来的？
How did the agent build it?

78
00:05:02,152 --> 00:05:07,400
周三凌晨 1 点 59 分，波士顿时间，它先把决策写了下来
On Wednesday at one fifty-nine in the morning, Boston time, it wrote the decision down.

79
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:12,114
17 分钟后，它提交了重做好的页面：27 个文件
Seventeen minutes later it committed the rebuilt page: 27 files.

80
00:05:12,434 --> 00:05:14,952
又过了 6 分钟，端到端测试也有了
Six minutes after that, end-to-end tests.

81
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,800
接下来是一轮又一轮的审查
Then came the reviews.

82
00:05:16,885 --> 00:05:18,741
一次独立的视觉审查
An independent visual review.

83
00:05:19,061 --> 00:05:23,328
你要的流式输出，做成了只流进度，以及对它的审查
Streaming, which you had asked for, built as progress only, and a review of it.

84
00:05:23,648 --> 00:05:26,883
第二轮视觉审查，带来了 Claude 的手机版排版
A second visual review, which brought Claude's phone layout

85
00:05:26,883 --> 00:05:30,283
以及你刚才看到的大部分家长用语和无障碍改动
and much of the parent wording and accessibility you just saw.

86
00:05:30,603 --> 00:05:33,052
最后是从五个角度做的终审
And a final review from five angles:

87
00:05:33,052 --> 00:05:37,814
约 30 个问题，在几条并行的分支上修好，然后又检查了一遍
about 30 problems, fixed on parallel branches, then checked once more.

88
00:05:38,050 --> 00:05:39,911
有一个 bug 能说明这件事为什么难
One bug shows why this is hard.

89
00:05:40,226 --> 00:05:44,386
发送和停止共用一个按钮：等回答的时候，发送变成停止
Send and stop share one button: while you wait, send turns into stop.

90
00:05:44,706 --> 00:05:46,237
点停止，等待结束
Click stop, the wait ends,

91
00:05:46,237 --> 00:05:49,476
就在同一次点击里，按钮又变回了发送
and in that same click the button turns back into send,

92
00:05:49,476 --> 00:05:51,597
于是输入框里的内容被发了出去
so whatever was in the box went out.

93
00:05:51,917 --> 00:05:55,543
在演示回放里，发出去的正是你刚刚停掉的那句话
In a demo replay, that was the very message you had just stopped.

94
00:05:55,863 --> 00:05:57,463
修复只有一行
The fix was one line.

95
00:05:57,613 --> 00:06:03,181
后来 Bugbot 又发现了它的镜像：双击发送，第二下点到了停止上
Then Bugbot found the mirror image: double-click send, and the second click lands on stop.

96
00:06:03,501 --> 00:06:07,405
又是一行修复：忽略双击的第二下
Another one-line fix: ignore the second click of a double-click.

97
00:06:07,725 --> 00:06:10,818
照抄一个按钮的样子，并不等于照抄了它的行为
Copying how a button looks does not copy how it behaves.

98
00:06:12,167 --> 00:06:14,279
大的聊天 app 有哪些我们没有的？
What do the big chat apps have that we don't?

99
00:06:14,599 --> 00:06:21,028
对话历史和项目、上传文件、语音、放文档和代码的侧边面板
Conversation history and projects, file uploads, voice, a side panel for documents and code,

100
00:06:21,028 --> 00:06:22,706
还有跨对话的记忆
and memory across chats.

101
00:06:23,026 --> 00:06:27,250
它们大多需要账号和存储，而这个原型没有
Most of them need accounts and storage, which this prototype doesn't have.

102
00:06:27,570 --> 00:06:29,816
这些里面，语音可能对这里最重要
Of these, voice may matter most here,

103
00:06:29,816 --> 00:06:33,094
着急的家长也许宁愿说话而不是打字；历史和记忆意味着要
for a worried parent who would rather speak than type;

104
00:06:33,094 --> 00:06:38,983
保存健康相关的对话，这要先做隐私上的决定
history and memory would mean keeping health conversations, which needs a privacy decision first.

105
00:06:39,217 --> 00:06:40,817
那只有我们能做的是什么？
And what could only we build?

106
00:06:41,052 --> 00:06:45,635
一个回答，两种读者：学生版和家长版并排放
One answer for two readers, the student's and the parent's, side by side;

107
00:06:45,635 --> 00:06:49,905
每条回答里已经有一段折叠起来的给家长的摘要，这就是雏形
every answer already carries a folded summary for parents, the seed.

108
00:06:50,225 --> 00:06:54,790
一张学生发回家的摘要卡片；复制给家长已经是第一步
A summary card the student sends home; copy for parent is already a first step.

109
00:06:55,110 --> 00:07:00,042
还有直接帮你预约：回答里已经写好了要说的英文句子
And a hand-off to booking: the answer already writes the English sentences to say;

110
00:07:00,042 --> 00:07:03,110
页面可以直接打电话，或者帮你填表
the page could place the call, or fill in the form.

111
00:07:03,350 --> 00:07:06,273
还有等你决定的：一共十几项
And what waits for you: a dozen open items.

112
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:08,779
决策 0006 仍然是提议
Decision six is still a proposal,

113
00:07:08,779 --> 00:07:12,753
agent 当晚在无人值守时补充的部分也是
and so is what the agent added to it that night, unattended:

114
00:07:12,753 --> 00:07:16,065
只流进度的流式输出、模型菜单和重新回答
progress-only streaming, the model menu and retry.

115
00:07:16,385 --> 00:07:18,351
还有两个选择需要你点头
Two more choices need your yes:

116
00:07:18,351 --> 00:07:23,046
停掉的那句话不再收回，而是和你的下一句一起发出去
a stopped message is no longer taken back but goes out with your next one,

117
00:07:23,046 --> 00:07:25,964
家长看到的危机热线没有拨号链接
and parents get no dial link for crisis lines.

118
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:30,259
所以：每个界面只照抄一个参考，一比一
So: one reference per screen, copied exactly,

119
00:07:30,259 --> 00:07:34,468
这样每个小选择都有答案，页面也让人觉得熟悉
so every small choice has an answer and the page feels familiar.

120
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:38,137
Claude 的版式、输入框和配色，只用在这一页
Claude's layout, composer and colours, kept to this page.

121
00:07:38,457 --> 00:07:43,001
不抄它的标志、历史、推理原文和逐字流式输出
Not its logo, its history, its raw thoughts or its word-by-word streaming.

122
00:07:43,321 --> 00:07:47,034
再加上只有一个面向两类读者的医疗页面才需要的东西
Plus what only a medical page for two audiences needs:

123
00:07:47,034 --> 00:07:50,747
紧急情况放最前、在中国的家长也能照着做的说法
emergency first, wording a parent in China can act on,

124
00:07:50,747 --> 00:07:53,497
以及跟着复制走的标注
and labels that travel with copied text.

125
00:07:53,733 --> 00:07:55,112
三个问题
Three questions.

126
00:07:55,162 --> 00:07:57,466
为什么照抄一个产品，而不是几个？
Why copy one product instead of several?

127
00:07:57,786 --> 00:08:01,328
为什么家长版的页面要请别人去打 911？
Why does the parent's page ask someone else to call 911?

128
00:08:01,648 --> 00:08:04,059
是什么让发送键两次变成了 bug？
And what turned the send key into a bug, twice?

129
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,019
下一集讲那两天本身
Next time: the two days themselves.

130
00:08:10,339 --> 00:08:13,411
agent 一个小时一个小时都做了什么，又花了多少钱
What the agents did, hour by hour, and what it cost.
